Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: mtk_eth_soc: backport per-conduit DSA queue
 map and PPE DSA refactor

Backport of Daniel Golle's pending "MxL862xx PPE offload" series from
OpenWrt main (target/linux/generic/pending-6.18/795-01 .. 795-07, 795-09)
to the 6.12 kernel used for the GL-BE14000:

  795-01 mtk_ppe_offload: use rhashtable_lookup_fast
  795-02 mtk_ppe: set tport_idx on netsys_v3 for QoS (Bo-Cun Chen)
  795-03 mtk_ppe_offload: set output device before VLAN/PPPoE push
  795-04 mtk_eth_soc: per-SoC QDMA TX queue count with register paging
  795-05 mtk_eth_soc: add per-conduit DSA user-port queue map
  795-06 mtk_eth_soc: use DSA queue map in TX paths
  795-07 mtk_ppe_offload: use DSA queue map in flow offload path
  795-09 mtk_ppe: push_vid out-parameter for mtk_flow_get_dsa_port() and
         ingress-side DSA user port -> conduit substitution

The BE14000 has two DSA switches on one MT7988 (built-in MT7530 on gmac0,
YT9224 on gmac1). Both number their user ports from 0, so with the old
"queue = dp->index + 3" rule the SFP+ port (YT9224 port 0) and lan5
(MT7530 port 0) share QDMA queue 3 and overwrite each other's rate
shaping. The queue map gives every user port its own queue.

Differences from the originals:
  - 795-08 (tag_mxl862xx_8021q) and the DSA_TAG_PROTO_MXL862_8021Q case
    of 795-09 are dropped; 6.12 has no MxL862xx tagger.
  - mtk_hw_dump() (OpenWrt debug code) converted from MTK_QDMA_NUM_QUEUES
    to soc->num_tx_queues.
  - mtk_add_mac() gains the loop variable the 6.18 function already had.

Drop this patch when the kernel base carries the series.
